# The enforcement surface. Replace @OWNER with a real human owner. The leading
# catch-all is deliberate: source-level mutation classifications and lint
# escapes can live anywhere, so every change needs the named owner's review.
# Enable the complete protected-branch checklist in README.md; CODEOWNERS alone
# does not dismiss stale approvals or prevent bypass. Cargo.toml is unanchored on purpose: member
# crate manifests carry the `[lints] workspace = true` opt-in, so adding one
# is a wall edit too. If the mise task fragment (20-rust.toml) lives outside
# /.config/mise/, add its path here.
* @OWNER
/.cargo/ @OWNER
/.config/mise/ @OWNER
/.github/ @OWNER
/AGENTS.md @OWNER
Cargo.toml @OWNER
/clippy.toml @OWNER
/deny.toml @OWNER
/rustfmt.toml @OWNER
